        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joel Chandler Harris, James Baskett, Uncle Remus\n- Characters and Works: Br'er Rabbit, Song of the South, Uncle Remus stories, \"Zip-a-Dee-Doo-Dah\"\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company\n\nFacts:\n- James Baskett was born on February 16, 1904.\n- Song of the South is based on the collection of Uncle Remus stories as adapted by Joel Chandler Harris.\n- The Walt Disney Company adapted Br'er Rabbit for its 1946 animated motion picture Song of the South.\n- In 1946, James Baskett portrayed Uncle Remus and sang \"Zip-a-Dee-Doo-Dah\" in the Disney feature film Song of the South.\n- James Baskett died on July 9, 1948.",
